<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $24.08 bln on March 7.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $24.08 bln on March 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $24.08 billion on March 7, 1997 from $23.67 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Mar 7	 Feb 28	 Mar 8</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     20,097	19,695	 16,134</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,977	 3,977	  4,659</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2	     21</p>
<p>    Total			     24,076	23,674	 20,814</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
